# Clearpay Customer Mobile — Design

## Product feel

- Modern, clean, trustworthy fintech UI
- Minimal visual noise
- Accessible contrast for text and status indicators
- Clear financial status signals (success / pending / failed / blocked)

## Brand language

Prefer the Clearpay navy / blue / teal palette defined in `tailwind.config.js`
(`navy`, `blue`, `teal`). Do not introduce arbitrary one-off colors for screens
or components.

## Implementation rules

- Build reusable primitives in `components/` before inventing screen-local UI
- Keep spacing and typography consistent across features
- Prefer NativeWind utilities aligned to the shared theme
- Use Lucide React Native for icons unless a brand asset is required
- Motion (Reanimated) should clarify hierarchy or feedback — not decorate

## Avoid

- Duplicated button / input / card patterns per feature
- Dense marketing clutter on transactional screens
- Low-contrast status colors for money and payment state
- Inventing a second design system alongside the shared tokens

## Design tooling

When exploring or refining UI, use available Design MCP / Mobbin references.
Keep approved visual decisions aligned with the shared theme tokens.
